config AK_ISP_CORE
	bool "Anyka ISP core, built from source"
	depends on ARCH_AK39
	help
	  The ak_isp_* implementation behind /dev/isp_char. Anyka ships this as
	  a prebuilt libispdrv.a per SoC; this builds it from the SDK sources
	  instead, adapted for this part.

	  The EV200 register-block sizes, word indices, SDB upload-enable bits in
	  REG5[32] and isp_working_mode numbering are applied and checked against
	  this unit's stock kernel. The port is still not finished: the 3A edits
	  are unapplied, the LUT blocks are unverified, and none of it has run on
	  hardware.

	  Depends on BROKEN so it cannot be enabled by accident. See
	  notes/isp-port.md for the remaining list.

	  If unsure, say N.

